## Fable at a glance

Fable is Playground Games' reboot of the Fable series, published by Xbox Game Studios. It is a new game set in Albion, not a remaster of the earlier Fable titles, and it has its own Steam listing. When we checked on 26 November 2026, both the official Steam page and Xbox's own Fable page gave the same release day: **23 February 2027**.

## What we know so far

- **Developer:** Playground Games. **Publisher:** Xbox Game Studios.
- **Release date:** 23 February 2027 on Steam and on Xbox.com.
- **Platforms:** Xbox's page lists Xbox console and PC, with Xbox Play Anywhere (buy once, play on both). It also says Fable is playable day one with Game Pass. The Steam version is Windows only.
- **Price on Steam (US):** $69.99 for the standard game, with a pre-order bonus pack (a Chicken Suit outfit and a few in-game gifts). The pre-order offer ends at launch.
- **Trailer:** the Steam page carries the Xbox Games Showcase 2026 trailer.
- **Languages:** full audio in English, German, Brazilian Portuguese and Latin American Spanish, plus several subtitle-only languages listed on Steam.

## What the game is about

The publisher describes Fable as an open-world action RPG in which you play the first Hero in a generation. The pitch centres on reputation: what you do changes how each villager treats you and can shape the world around you. The official tagline sums up the tone: "Fairytale Ending Not Guaranteed."

Combat mixes melee, ranged attacks and magic, and you can customise your Hero's appearance. The store page names both new enemies and returning series creatures, including Hobbes, Balverines and Trolls.

Outside combat, the listing describes a life-simulation side familiar from earlier Fable games. You can earn money as a landlord or blacksmith, romance villagers, and raise children. The publisher says your power grows alongside your reputation, so the two halves of the game are meant to feed each other.

## PC details from the Steam listing

Steam lists these requirements. Both tiers need Windows 10 22H2, DirectX 12, 135 GB of storage and an SSD.

- **Minimum:** AMD Ryzen 5 2600 or Intel i7-6850K, 12 GB RAM, and an AMD Radeon RX 6600, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 or Intel Arc A580 class graphics card.
- **Recommended:** AMD Ryzen 5 5600 or Intel i5-11600KF, 16 GB RAM, and an AMD Radeon RX 6700 XT or NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti.

The publisher also lists uncapped frame rates, 4K HDR10 output, and optional NVIDIA DLSS 4.5, AMD FSR 3 and 4, and Intel XeSS 2.1 on supported hardware. Full controller support is listed, and a gamepad is recommended.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Performance:** nobody outside the studio has a final build. The requirements above are the publisher's targets, not measured results. We have not played or benchmarked Fable.
- **Other consoles:** the Xbox and Steam pages we checked don't mention PlayStation or Nintendo versions. Check the publisher's announcements if you play on another console.
- **Length and size of the world:** neither listing gives a campaign length or map size, so we don't quote one.
- **The date itself:** 23 February 2027 is the date the publisher showed on 26 November 2026. Release dates can still change.

## How to follow it

Use the Steam app for this game (ID 2769570) or Xbox's Fable page, not an older Fable store page. Several earlier Fable games are still sold under similar names, so an old listing can show up in search results.

